From 609763f6e2ec8741bcdb8d072fc17a65e41290f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 13:26:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] Do not let a synthesised PANOSE byte travel as the
 document's own word
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

panose/defaultName now gate on source_format == FileFormat::Hwp (the CFB/OLE
binary path) and are omitted entirely on every other path, instead of passing
through whatever Font.type_info/default_name happens to hold.

Why the gate has to be on FORMAT, not on emptiness: on HWP5, both fields are
copied straight from file bytes (parser/doc_info.rs, no interpretation). On
HWPX, neither is trustworthy as "the document's own PANOSE" — default_name
never reads the file at all (rhwp's own hwp5_default_font_name lookup table),
and type_info's byte 1 (serif style) is rhwp's synthesize_serif_type name
guess, since HWPX's <hh:typeInfo> has no attribute for that byte. Byte 0
(familyType) DOES come from a real XML attribute, but font_family_type_to_u8
renumbers Hancom's FCAT_MYUNGJO/FCAT_GOTHIC/... strings 1-7 in declaration
order, which is not standard PANOSE bFamilyType (0 Any/1 No Fit/2 Latin
Text/3 Script/4 Decorative/5 Pictorial) - so even the "real" byte doesn't
mean what a PANOSE-literate consumer would assume. A consumer that ranked
this above its own morpheme-based inference, believing it was honouring the
document, would in fact be laundering the parser's guess above rhwp's own
guess-with-measurement (invariant 57).

Whole-block omission loses nothing actionable: whether an HWPX document had
no <hh:typeInfo> at all or one this exporter cannot trust, the intended
downstream behaviour is identical - fall back to morpheme inference. Format
is decided once per document (detect_format, magic bytes: CFB/OLE -> Hwp,
ZIP -> Hwpx), not by extension, so an .hwpx-named file whose bytes are
actually HWP5 binary correctly keeps its real PANOSE - verified against 5
such fixtures under samples/issue1891, samples/task1768, samples/task2097.

export_s2_font_table_fields updated: HWP5 sample still asserts real bytes:
the 2025 행정업무운영 편람(최종) HWPX edition now asserts panose/defaultName
are BOTH absent, not present-with-a-different-value.

Verified with a recursive scan of every .hwpx under samples/ (254 files):
zero leak panose or defaultName after this change.
